        "original_id": "a15349cd-d50c-5663-8cc0-20aa271c06c6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush, Roger Taylor, Taylor Hawkins, Lisa Carver\n- Music Groups: Sugarland, Soul Miner's Daughter, Jennifer Nettles Band, Foo Fighters\n- Songs and Albums: \"Everyday America\", Love on the Inside\n- Companies: Mercury Nashville Records, Planet Rock\n\nFacts:\n- Before Sugarland was formed, Jennifer Nettles fronted the Atlanta-based bands Soul Miner's Daughter and Jennifer Nettles Band.\n- In 2005, Planet Rock radio listeners voted Roger Taylor the eighth-greatest drummer in classic rock music history.\n- In 2008, Sugarland released its third studio album, Love on the Inside, on Mercury Nashville Records.\n- Jennifer Nettles is best known as the lead singer of the duo Sugarland alongside Kristian Bush.\n- Taylor Hawkins of Foo Fighters praised Roger Taylor as one of the most influential rock drummers of the 1970s and 1980s.\n- \"Everyday America\" was written by Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush, and Lisa Carver.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cf0b7791-6bb1-58b8-b02b-ec262f3118b4",
        "text": "Page: Jennifer Nettles. Sentence: She is best known as the lead singer of the duo Sugarland alongside Kristian Bush.\nPage: Jennifer Nettles. Sentence: Before Sugarland's inception, she also fronted Atlanta-based bands called Soul Miner's Daughter and Jennifer Nettles Band.\nPage: Roger Taylor (Queen drummer). Sentence: He has been acclaimed by Foo Fighters drummer Taylor Hawkins as one of the most influential rock drummers of the 1970s and 1980s, as well as being voted by radio listeners as the eighth-greatest drummer in classic rock music history in a poll conducted by Planet Rock in 2005.\nPage: Everyday America. Sentence: It was written by Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush and Lisa Carver.\nPage: Love on the Inside. Sentence: Love on the Inside is the third studio album by American country music duo Sugarland, released in 2008 (see 2008 in country music) on Mercury Nashville Records.",
